lla","dish/panella"],["Pani câ meusa","dish/pani-ca-meusa"],["Parmigiana","dish/parmigiana"],["Pasta alla Norma","dish/pasta-alla-norma"],["Pasta con le sarde","dish/pasta-con-le-sarde"],["Pasta mollicata","dish/pasta-mollicata"],["Stigghiola","dish/stigghiola"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/bb/Cassatelle_di_Agira_3.jpg/500px-Cassatelle_di_Agira_3.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Auregann","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassatelle_di_Agira_3.jpg"}},"ingredient/raspberry-jam":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/raspberry-jam","n":"Raspberry jam","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Fruit preserves are preparations of fruits whose main preserving agent is sugar and sometimes acid, often stored in glass jars and used as a condiment or spread."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-raspberry-jam"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry_jam"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Apples","ingredient/apples"],["Malic acid","ingredient/malic-acid"],["Raspberries","ingredient/raspberries"],["Shortbread","ingredient/shortbread"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"],["Strawberries","ingredient/strawberries"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tartaric acid","ingredient/tartaric-acid"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}]},"ingredient/kibbeh":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/kibbeh","n":"Kibbeh","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Kibbeh is a popular dish in the Arab world and the Levant in particular, made of spiced lean ground meat and bulgur wheat. Kibbeh is considered to be a national dish of Lebanon and Syria."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kibbeh"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kibbeh"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Arab cuisine","cuisine/arab-cuisine",[["Kibbeh safarjaliyeh","dish/kibbeh-safarjaliyeh"]]],["Levantine cuisine","cuisine/levantine-cuisine",[["Kibbeh safarjaliyeh","dish/kibbeh-safarjaliyeh"]]],["Syrian cuisine","cuisine/syrian-cuisine",[["Kibbeh safarjaliyeh","dish/kibbeh-safarjaliyeh"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Pomegranate","ingredient/pomegranate"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/8/88/Kibbeh3.jpg/500px-Kibbeh3.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Basel15 at the English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kibbeh3.jpg"}},"dish/raclette":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/raclette","n":"Raclette","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Swiss cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Raclette is a dish of Swiss origin, also popular in other countries, based on heating cheese and scraping off the melted part, then typically served with boiled potatoes. Raclette is historically a dish originating from the canton of Valais in Switzerland. This cheese from Valais benefits from an AOP. Raclette cheese is also a Swiss-type cheese marketed specifically to be used for this dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-raclette"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raclette"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Raclette du Valais","ingredient/raclette-du-valais"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with not