 also be used."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-riz-casimir"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riz_Casimir"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Curry powder","ingredient/curry-powder"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with notes on Swiss cookbooks.","url":"https://www.helvetickitchen.com/recipes/retrospective","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Cuisine Helvetica","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cuisinehelvetica.com","note":"Heddi Nieuwsma's Swiss recipes and food culture from her life in Switzerland.","url":"https://cuisinehelvetica.com/swiss-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Swiss cuisine","links":[["Älplermagronen","dish/alplermagronen"],["Basler Läckerli","dish/basler-lackerli"],["Birnbrot","dish/birnbrot"],["Bündnerfleisch","dish/bundnerfleisch"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Carac (pastry)","dish/carac-pastry"],["Cervelat","dish/cervelat"],["Cholera (food)","dish/cholera-food"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Raclette","dish/raclette"],["Schenkele","dish/schenkele"],["Spätzle","dish/spatzle"],["Swiss sausages and cured meats","dish/swiss-sausages-and-cured-meats"],["Wähe","dish/wahe"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"],["Zuger Kirschtorte","dish/zuger-kirschtorte"],["Zürcher Geschnetzeltes","dish/zurcher-geschnetzeltes"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/3/3b/Riz_Casimir_%284247740294%29.jpg","w":500,"h":325,"by":"kochtopf","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Riz_Casimir_(4247740294).jpg"}},"ingredient/pulse-legume":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pulse-legume","n":"Pulse (legume)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Legumes are plants in the pea family Fabaceae (or Leguminosae), or the fruit or seeds of such plants. When used as a dry grain for human consumption, the seeds are also called pulses. Legumes are grown agriculturally, primarily for human consumption, but also as livestock forage and silage, and as soil-enhancing green manure. Legumes produce a botanically unique type of fruit—a simple dry fruit that develops from a simple carpel and usually dehisces (opens along a seam) on two sides."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pulse-legume"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulse_(legume)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine",[["Scotch broth","dish/scotch-broth"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Barley","ingredient/barley"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Rutabaga","ingredient/rutabaga"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/e/e7/Various_legumes.jpg/500px-Various_legumes.jpg","w":500,"h":748,"by":"Keith Weller, Agricultural Research Service, USDA","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Various_legumes.jpg"}},"dish/strong-beer":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/strong-beer","n":"Strong beer","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Strong beer is a term for beer that is in some way more potent than regular beer. The concept is only generally used in some countries, and local tax laws often define what constitutes strong beer."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-strong-beer"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stron